      "dcterms:description": "{\"action\":\"\",\"actor\":\"\",\"alternative_quotes\":[],\"applies_to\":[],\"assertion_ids\":[\"urn:rulespec:document-understanding:assertion:1148f8f969d26937f2f924abd361441ed46ed3a71176e94e98cef53af15ec0d6\",\"urn:rulespec:document-understanding:assertion:9e0fc97e3610fba5a8a71d08b4bf2426e65f9ace24cdeac3fffc5b0ce89e4ff7\",\"urn:rulespec:document-understanding:assertion:d8fadb8064fc18b2d32e267278557fcf6db3cb16fba5183ed151d8e3f277268a\",\"urn:rulespec:document-understanding:assertion:6269844055618ee2b0df5b9b28b7dfea1b67abc42acae6f71232c6d446f4738a\",\"urn:rulespec:document-understanding:assertion:6bc3b45b8f805903eece2dde4b8cf5895dbab9d1ed47edd2e359e5d10918023d\"],\"choice_quote\":\"\",\"choice_text\":\"\",\"claimants\":[],\"concepts\":[],\"context_quotes\":[\"(d) The determination of whether an employee meets the hours of service requirement and has been employed by the employer for a total of at least 12 months must be made as of the date the FMLA leave is to start. An employee may be on non-FMLA leave at the time he or she meets the 12-month eligibility requirement, and in that event, any portion of the leave taken for an FMLA-qualifying reason after the employee meets the eligibility requirement would be FMLA leave. See § 825.300(b) for rules governing the content of the eligibility notice given to employees.\"],\"effective_periods\":[],\"end\":5933,\"evidence\":[{\"end\":5933,\"field\":\"summary\",\"fragment_id\":\"urn:rkaf:fragment:urn%3Arulespec%3Adocument-understanding%3Adocument%3Aa4cdfc9b75c8a1ed78c29b8a344913757e4b95198a4b069127aa9092960aaf4f:5370:5933:sha256-47eba493b53486ba093d7a6299a7e50e0816dd5ddeb5de830bd5be07e6f5395c\",\"quote\":\"(d) The determination of whether an employee meets the hours of service requirement and has been employed by the employer for a total of at least 12 months must be made as of the date the FMLA leave is to start. An employee may be on non-FMLA leave at the time he or she meets the 12-month eligibility requirement, and in that event, any portion of the leave taken for an FMLA-qualifying reason after the employee meets the eligibility requirement would be FMLA leave. See § 825.300(b) for rules governing the content of the eligibility notice given to employees.\",\"start\":5370},{\"end\":5933,\"field\":\"logic_text\",\"fragment_id\":\"urn:rkaf:fragment:urn%3Arulespec%3Adocument-understanding%3Adocument%3Aa4cdfc9b75c8a1ed78c29b8a344913757e4b95198a4b069127aa9092960aaf4f:5370:5933:sha256-47eba493b53486ba093d7a6299a7e50e0816dd5ddeb5de830bd5be07e6f5395c\",\"quote\":\"(d) The determination of whether an employee meets the hours of service requirement and has been employed by the employer for a total of at least 12 months must be made as of the date the FMLA leave is to start. An employee may be on non-FMLA leave at the time he or she meets the 12-month eligibility requirement, and in that event, any portion of the leave taken for an FMLA-qualifying reason after the employee meets the eligibility requirement would be FMLA leave. See § 825.300(b) for rules governing the content of the eligibility notice given to employees.\",\"start\":5370},{\"end\":5530,\"field\":\"modality\",\"fragment_id\":\"urn:rkaf:fragment:urn%3Arulespec%3Adocument-understanding%3Adocument%3Aa4cdfc9b75c8a1ed78c29b8a344913757e4b95198a4b069127aa9092960aaf4f:5526:5530:sha256-4137b01e139589b7a1d3b3fc4da031d8ce5bb415808734e970c3a58ea0e98f0f\",\"quote\":\"must\",\"start\":5526},{\"end\":5933,\"field\":\"scope_text:0\",\"fragment_id\":\"urn:rkaf:fragment:urn%3Arulespec%3Adocument-understanding%3Adocument%3Aa4cdfc9b75c8a1ed78c29b8a344913757e4b95198a4b069127aa9092960aaf4f:5370:5933:sha256-47eba493b53486ba093d7a6299a7e50e0816dd5ddeb5de830bd5be07e6f5395c\",\"quote\":\"(d) The determination of whether an employee meets the hours of service requirement and has been employed by the employer for a total of at least 12 months must be made as of the date the FMLA leave is to start. An employee may be on non-FMLA leave at the time he or she meets the 12-month eligibility requirement, and in that event, any portion of the leave taken for an FMLA-qualifying reason after the employee meets the eligibility requirement would be FMLA leave. See § 825.300(b) for rules governing the content of the eligibility notice given to employees.\",\"start\":5370},{\"end\":5933,\"field\":\"context:0\",\"fragment_id\":\"urn:rkaf:fragment:urn%3Arulespec%3Adocument-understanding%3Adocument%3Aa4cdfc9b75c8a1ed78c29b8a344913757e4b95198a4b069127aa9092960aaf4f:5370:5933:sha256-47eba493b53486ba093d7a6299a7e50e0816dd5ddeb5de830bd5be07e6f5395c\",\"quote\":\"(d) The determination of whether an employee meets the hours of service requirement and has been employed by the employer for a total of at least 12 months must be made as of the date the FMLA leave is to start. An employee may be on non-FMLA leave at the time he or she meets the 12-month eligibility requirement, and in that event, any portion of the leave taken for an FMLA-qualifying reason after the employee meets the eligibility requirement would be FMLA leave. See § 825.300(b) for rules governing the content of the eligibility notice given to employees.\",\"start\":5370}],\"id\":\"urn:rulespec:document-understanding:revision:2d050e1cc41bc22c830f8e39f35152142a332bb93468c0e1bfc4e5d5773431e7\",\"jurisdiction\":\"\",\"jurisdiction_quote\":\"\",\"kind\":\"requirement\",\"logic_text\":\"(d) The determination of whether an employee meets the hours of service requirement and has been employed by the employer for a total of at least 12 months must be made as of the date the FMLA leave is to start. An employee may be on non-FMLA leave at the time he or she meets the 12-month eligibility requirement, and in that event, any portion of the leave taken for an FMLA-qualifying reason after the employee meets the eligibility requirement would be FMLA leave. See § 825.300(b) for rules governing the content of the eligibility notice given to employees.\",\"meaning_assertion_id\":\"urn:rulespec:document-understanding:assertion:6bc3b45b8f805903eece2dde4b8cf5895dbab9d1ed47edd2e359e5d10918023d\",\"modality\":\"must\",\"modality_quote\":\"must\",\"object\":\"\",\"occurrence_id\":\"urn:rulespec:document-understanding:occurrence:76a69a80aa20afbaa090620ce6dfe44254d2c4030d2668b26c593daaf48c0b2e\",\"origin\":\"aiSuggested\",\"quote\":\"(d) The determination of whether an employee meets the hours of service requirement and has been employed by the employer for a total of at least 12 months must be made as of the date the FMLA leave is to start. An employee may be on non-FMLA leave at the time he or she meets the 12-month eligibility requirement, and in that event, any portion of the leave taken for an FMLA-qualifying reason after the employee meets the eligibility requirement would be FMLA leave. See § 825.300(b) for rules governing the content of the eligibility notice given to employees.\",\"references\":[\"§ 825.300(b)\"],\"relation\":\"none\",\"rule_id\":\"urn:rulespec:document-understanding:rule:c2747d3daf40ae1608737a9859120c4b624ed35f3143dfbfb950d8514903f693\",\"scope_quotes\":[\"(d) The determination of whether an employee meets the hours of service requirement and has been employed by the employer for a total of at least 12 months must be made as of the date the FMLA leave is to start. An employee may be on non-FMLA leave at the time he or she meets the 12-month eligibility requirement, and in that event, any portion of the leave taken for an FMLA-qualifying reason after the employee meets the eligibility requirement would be FMLA leave. See § 825.300(b) for rules governing the content of the eligibility notice given to employees.\"],\"scope_text\":\"When making the determination of whether an employee meets the hours of service requirement and has been employed by the employer for a total of at least 12 months.\",\"section_id\":\"section-1\",\"start\":5370,\"summary\":\"The determination of whether an employee meets the hours of service requirement and has been employed by the employer for a total of at least 12 months must be made as of the date the FMLA leave is to start.\",\"target_ids\":[],\"typed_values\":[]}",
