    {
      "@id": "urn:rulespec:document-understanding:revision:3e8b4934ef99983a80863938e22930b6ce24efcd0dad26ab67832035bbc4dcc9",
      "@type": "rkaf:Artifact",
      "rkaf:hasArtifactIdentifier": "urn:rulespec:document-understanding:revision:3e8b4934ef99983a80863938e22930b6ce24efcd0dad26ab67832035bbc4dcc9",
      "rkaf:artifactIdentifierScheme": "rkaf:urn-persistent",
      "rkaf:hasContentDigest": "sha256:7ca563cba6dc81c9fcaed0eed042fb85bb964796cfa0325bc77618f104a23a1d",
      "dcterms:format": "application/json",
      "dcterms:description": "{\"action\":\"\",\"actor\":\"\",\"alternative_quotes\":[],\"applies_to\":[],\"assertion_ids\":[\"urn:rulespec:document-understanding:assertion:e16103eb63ac9e140e91e1206e012a2774033804f7428ead5ac960d54ea242bc\",\"urn:rulespec:document-understanding:assertion:5b4e5af117d90335d406bafa5f513863a4183b57c08146f26bc6c7c3ce54c8e6\",\"urn:rulespec:document-understanding:assertion:38003245e7875586d36b82632a5ded3f37462a5daaa3e425276b33b5ede6b7df\",\"urn:rulespec:document-understanding:assertion:9a285cfaf43eb87dfb4c8af1b22d6ab08e653dcff60eba889fa775ea1f17e541\",\"urn:rulespec:document-understanding:assertion:a5130d32c4c580a7ba35e49df56436dd7af472831569482eb545a86d5a272168\"],\"choice_quote\":\"\",\"choice_text\":\"\",\"claimants\":[],\"concepts\":[],\"context_quotes\":[\"(d) The determination of whether an employee meets the hours of service requirement and has been employed by the employer for a total of at least 12 months must be made as of the date the FMLA leave is to start. An employee may be on non-FMLA leave at the time he or she meets the 12-month eligibility requirement, and in that event, any portion of the leave taken for an FMLA-qualifying reason after the employee meets the eligibility requirement would be FMLA leave. See § 825.300(b) for rules governing the content of the eligibility notice given to employees.\"],\"effective_periods\":[],\"end\":5933,\"evidence\":[{\"end\":5933,\"field\":\"summary\",\"fragment_id\":\"urn:rkaf:fragment:urn%3Arulespec%3Adocument-understanding%3Adocument%3Aa4cdfc9b75c8a1ed78c29b8a344913757e4b95198a4b069127aa9092960aaf4f:5370:5933:sha256-47eba493b53486ba093d7a6299a7e50e0816dd5ddeb5de830bd5be07e6f5395c\",\"quote\":\"(d) The determination of whether an employee meets the hours of service requirement and has been employed by the employer for a total of at least 12 months must be made as of the date the FMLA leave is to start. An employee may be on non-FMLA leave at the time he or she meets the 12-month eligibility requirement, and in that event, any portion of the leave taken for an FMLA-qualifying reason after the employee meets the eligibility requirement would be FMLA leave. See § 825.300(b) for rules governing the content of the eligibility notice given to employees.\",\"start\":5370},{\"end\":5933,\"field\":\"logic_text\",\"fragment_id\":\"urn:rkaf:fragment:urn%3Arulespec%3Adocument-understanding%3Adocument%3Aa4cdfc9b75c8a1ed78c29b8a344913757e4b95198a4b069127aa9092960aaf4f:5370:5933:sha256-47eba493b53486ba093d7a6299a7e50e0816dd5ddeb5de830bd5be07e6f5395c\",\"quote\":\"(d) The determination of whether an employee meets the hours of service requirement and has been employed by the employer for a total of at least 12 months must be made as of the date the FMLA leave is to start. An employee may be on non-FMLA leave at the time he or she meets the 12-month eligibility requirement, and in that event, any portion of the leave taken for an FMLA-qualifying reason after the employee meets the eligibility requirement would be FMLA leave. See § 825.300(b) for rules governing the content of the eligibility notice given to employees.\",\"start\":5370},{\"end\":5826,\"field\":\"modality\",\"fragment_id\":\"urn:rkaf:fragment:urn%3Arulespec%3Adocument-understanding%3Adocument%3Aa4cdfc9b75c8a1ed78c29b8a344913757e4b95198a4b069127aa9092960aaf4f:5818:5826:sha256-a50f07f21884286fddcfbf38061df13ec07741f4fba1fd0300667235260359cc\",\"quote\":\"would be\",\"start\":5818},{\"end\":5933,\"field\":\"scope_text:0\",\"fragment_id\":\"urn:rkaf:fragment:urn%3Arulespec%3Adocument-understanding%3Adocument%3Aa4cdfc9b75c8a1ed78c29b8a344913757e4b95198a4b069127aa9092960aaf4f:5370:5933:sha256-47eba493b53486ba093d7a6299a7e50e0816dd5ddeb5de830bd5be07e6f5395c\",\"quote\":\"(d) The determination of whether an employee meets the hours of service requirement and has been employed by the employer for a total of at least 12 months must be made as of the date the FMLA leave is to start. An employee may be on non-FMLA leave at the time he or she meets the 12-month eligibility requirement, and in that event, any portion of the leave taken for an FMLA-qualifying reason after the employee meets the eligibility requirement would be FMLA leave. See § 825.300(b) for rules governing the content of the eligibility notice given to employees.\",\"start\":5370},{\"end\":5933,\"field\":\"context:0\",\"fragment_id\":\"urn:rkaf:fragment:urn%3Arulespec%3Adocument-understanding%3Adocument%3Aa4cdfc9b75c8a1ed78c29b8a344913757e4b95198a4b069127aa9092960aaf4f:5370:5933:sha256-47eba493b53486ba093d7a6299a7e50e0816dd5ddeb5de830bd5be07e6f5395c\",\"quote\":\"(d) The determination of whether an employee meets the hours of service requirement and has been employed by the employer for a total of at least 12 months must be made as of the date the FMLA leave is to start. An employee may be on non-FMLA leave at the time he or she meets the 12-month eligibility requirement, and in that event, any portion of the leave taken for an FMLA-qualifying reason after the employee meets the eligibility requirement would be FMLA leave. See § 825.300(b) for rules governing the content of the eligibility notice given to employees.\",\"start\":5370}],\"id\":\"urn:rulespec:document-understanding:revision:3e8b4934ef99983a80863938e22930b6ce24efcd0dad26ab67832035bbc4dcc9\",\"jurisdiction\":\"\",\"jurisdiction_quote\":\"\",\"kind\":\"statement\",\"logic_text\":\"(d) The determination of whether an employee meets the hours of service requirement and has been employed by the employer for a total of at least 12 months must be made as of the date the FMLA leave is to start. An employee may be on non-FMLA leave at the time he or she meets the 12-month eligibility requirement, and in that event, any portion of the leave taken for an FMLA-qualifying reason after the employee meets the eligibility requirement would be FMLA leave. See § 825.300(b) for rules governing the content of the eligibility notice given to employees.\",\"meaning_assertion_id\":\"urn:rulespec:document-understanding:assertion:a5130d32c4c580a7ba35e49df56436dd7af472831569482eb545a86d5a272168\",\"modality\":\"not_stated\",\"modality_quote\":\"would be\",\"object\":\"\",\"occurrence_id\":\"urn:rulespec:document-understanding:occurrence:1966e16da403daf1a8db0e3ace2e9115385910b17f501beac7c49b8e4504a6a4\",\"origin\":\"aiSuggested\",\"quote\":\"(d) The determination of whether an employee meets the hours of service requirement and has been employed by the employer for a total of at least 12 months must be made as of the date the FMLA leave is to start. An employee may be on non-FMLA leave at the time he or she meets the 12-month eligibility requirement, and in that event, any portion of the leave taken for an FMLA-qualifying reason after the employee meets the eligibility requirement would be FMLA leave. See § 825.300(b) for rules governing the content of the eligibility notice given to employees.\",\"references\":[\"§ 825.300(b)\"],\"relation\":\"none\",\"rule_id\":\"urn:rulespec:document-understanding:rule:9d1d84d863e87a88ef21d352979f2b29f6dc8ad6d02d79f5e80cbf478d0a9248\",\"scope_quotes\":[\"(d) The determination of whether an employee meets the hours of service requirement and has been employed by the employer for a total of at least 12 months must be made as of the date the FMLA leave is to start. An employee may be on non-FMLA leave at the time he or she meets the 12-month eligibility requirement, and in that event, any portion of the leave taken for an FMLA-qualifying reason after the employee meets the eligibility requirement would be FMLA leave. See § 825.300(b) for rules governing the content of the eligibility notice given to employees.\"],\"scope_text\":\"When an employee is on non-FMLA leave at the time he or she meets the 12-month eligibility requirement.\",\"section_id\":\"section-1\",\"start\":5370,\"summary\":\"An employee may be on non-FMLA leave at the time he or she meets the 12-month eligibility requirement, and in that event, any portion of the leave taken for an FMLA-qualifying reason after the employee meets the eligibility requirement would be FMLA leave.\",\"target_ids\":[],\"typed_values\":[]}",
      "dcterms:references": [
        {
          "@id": "urn:rulespec:document-understanding:assertion:e16103eb63ac9e140e91e1206e012a2774033804f7428ead5ac960d54ea242bc"
